<h2 class="section-heading">Core TM7 Accessories</h2>
<p class="section-subheading">Prices reflect Vorwerk's listed pricing — click through to my link for the current price and any active bundle.</p>
<div class="feature-grid">
  <div class="feature">
    <img class="accessory-image" src="https://www.thermomix.ca/cdn/shop/files/TM7Cutter_fullset.jpg" alt="Thermomix Cutter+ attachment and blades" loading="lazy">
    <h3>Cutter+</h3>
    <p><strong>~$199 CAD.</strong> Turns the TM7 into a mandoline, spiralizer, and grater — ribbons, noodles, or shredded cheese straight into the bowl. Worth it for salads and veg-forward cooking. Often discounted when bundled with a new TM7 — see <a href="/#promotions">current promotions</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <img class="accessory-image" src="https://www.thermomix.ca/cdn/shop/files/Bladecoverandpeeler.jpg" alt="Thermomix Blade Cover and Peeler" loading="lazy">
    <h3>Blade Cover & Peeler</h3>
    <p><strong>~$59 CAD.</strong> A 3-in-1 attachment: peels vegetables, covers the blades so you can slow-cook or sous vide without them spinning, and lets you safely handle, wash, and store the blades without touching the sharp edges directly.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <img class="accessory-image" src="https://www.thermomix.ca/cdn/shop/files/230.jpg" alt="Thermomix Sensor wireless probe thermometer" loading="lazy">
    <h3>Thermomix Sensor</h3>
    <p><strong>~$169 CAD.</strong> A wireless probe thermometer that reports internal temperature straight to the TM7 screen — ideal for proteins, candy, or sous vide where "done" means a specific number.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <img class="accessory-image" src="https://www.thermomix.ca/cdn/shop/files/TM7_Mixing_Bowl_2.png" alt="TM7 spare mixing bowl" loading="lazy">
    <h3>TM7 Mixing Bowl (Complete)</h3>
    <p><strong>~$350 CAD.</strong> A full spare bowl assembly — the same insulated, heated bowl that ships with the TM7. Useful for batch-cooking a second recipe while the first runs, or as a replacement.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <img class="accessory-image" src="https://www.thermomix.ca/cdn/shop/files/TM7trolley.jpg" alt="TM7 rolling trolley cart" loading="lazy">
    <h3>TM7 Trolley</h3>
    <p><strong>~$199 CAD.</strong> A rolling cart sized for the TM7 and its accessories — handy in small kitchens without permanent counter space, or for moving the machine to events.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature">
    <img class="accessory-image" src="https://www.thermomix.ca/cdn/shop/files/24.Thermomix_CarryBag.jpg" alt="Thermomix TM7 padded carry bag" loading="lazy">
    <h3>TM7 Carry Bag</h3>
    <p><strong>~$89 CAD.</strong> A padded case for the TM7 and its accessories — good for cottage weekends, a second home, or between demos.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <h2>Do You Need Any of This to Get Started?</h2>
  <p>No. Every TM7 already ships with the mixing bowl, Varoma steaming set, spatula, butterfly whisk, and simmering basket — enough to cook the vast majority of Cookidoo recipes. Treat this page as an upgrade list, not a shopping requirement. In our house, the Cutter+ gets the most actual use — it's what makes prepping a stir-fry or salad for five people fast enough on a weeknight. The dough mat comes out whenever we're making dumplings from scratch. The trolley and carry bag, honestly, sit in the box — our TM7 lives on the counter and never leaves.</p>
</div>

